Fluxnova
--------

Fluxnova is published by FINOS in
https://github.com/finos/fluxnova-bpm-platform under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. Its NOTICE reads, in part:

  Fluxnova - FINOS
  Copyright 2013-2025 Camunda Services GmbH
  Copyright 2025 - FINOS info@finos.org

  This product includes software developed at the Fintech Open Source
  Foundation (https://www.finos.org/).

src/fluxnova_bpm_platform/schema/ models the engine's database tables, from the
H2 DDL, and the BPMN model API, from its registerType methods, at Fluxnova
3.1.1 (tag v3.1.1, commit 3ac64ca2c3d7c93f00395e18b9dc3218e5250264).
scripts/upstream_pins.tsv lists every file of FINOS's tree the converters read.
The schema's structure is this project's. Where an engine class or slot has a
description, its first sentence is taken from the Javadoc of the engine's Java
API, and is FINOS's and Camunda's words. The BPMN descriptions, in
scripts/bpmn_descriptions.yaml, are this project's. Table and column names,
element and attribute names, namespaces, and the state codes and values the
engine defines are Fluxnova's. src/fluxnova_bpm_platform/datamodel/, project/
and docs/schema/ are generated from the schema.

BPMN
----

BPMN 2.0 is a specification of the Object Management Group (OMG). The schema
names BPMN's elements by the XML names and namespaces that Fluxnova's model API
registers, and maps each to that name. bpmn_to_linkml.py reads the BPMN XML
Schema the model API ships in FINOS's tree only to find which elements hold
text; no text of the specification is copied here. OMG, BPMN and their logos
are OMG's.

FINOS, its logo and Fluxnova's name are FINOS's. This project is not a FINOS
project, and its use of them does not imply FINOS's or OMG's endorsement.

